   Goal:   Host a custom validator component and surface its own messages.
   Drills: EditForm hosting a validator, OnValidSubmit/OnInvalidSubmit(EditContext), tallying submits.
   Passes: dotnet test --filter FullyQualifiedName~Ex041_ *@
@* TODO: render <EditForm Model="Model" OnValidSubmit="HandleValid" OnInvalidSubmit="HandleInvalid">
   containing <Ex041_CustomFieldValidation_Validator />, an <InputText id="name"
   @bind-Value="Model.Name" />, a <div id="name-errors"><ValidationMessage For="() =>
   Model.Name" /></div>, and a submit button #submit; below the form a <ul id="errors">
   with one <li> per message from the EditContext's GetValidationMessages(), and a
   <span id="counts">@ValidCount/@InvalidCount</span>. Both OnValidSubmit and
   OnInvalidSubmit are EventCallback<EditContext> - each hands you the very EditContext
   that was just validated, so capture it in a field rather than building or requesting
   one of your own. The #name-errors div is what actually exercises the validator's
   FieldIdentifier choice: ValidationMessage only shows a message that was added under
   the exact FieldIdentifier its For expression resolves to - get that identifier wrong
   in the validator and #name-errors stays empty even though the unscoped #errors list
   still shows it. *@

